  "question": {
    "text": "A planet of radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo></math> (radius of Earth) has the same mass density as Earth. Scientists dig a well of depth <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> on it and lower a wire of the same length and of linear mass density <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> into it. If the wire is not touching anywhere, the force applied at the top of the wire by a person holding it in place is (take the radius of Earth <math><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and the acceleration due to gravity of Earth is <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )",
    "image": null
  },
